<section class="border-t border-line" aria-labelledby="switching-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="switching-title" class="h2">
        Moving from another tracker, with you checking the map.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5 max-w-[46ch]">
        Connect the same agent to your current tracker and to Nothing Left. It reads the unresolved work there, proposes
        how people, fields and tags map across, and creates the issues here once you approve.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7">
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="prompt">
          <span class="mark">›</span>
          <span>
            Find the unresolved issues in my YouTrack project, show me the proposed people, field and tag mapping, then
            create them in Nothing Left after I approve.
          </span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="prose mt-6 text-base">
        This is a guided migration by prompt, not a one-click importer. Source access, field mapping, duplicates,
        attachments, history and who is who all need your review. For a bulk move, use the generic CSV import.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
